96284c7d-216b-471c-9b88-8e5813245873	acme-data-migration-20d649	requirements	PRD-D5-01	## Objective / Summary\nD5 classifies incoming Jira tickets as in-scope, out-of-scope, or ambiguous against the\nparsed SOW. Original build (KPD-5 epic) shipped classification with only two buckets\n(in-scope / out-of-scope), which PM feedback flagged almost immediately as unusable —\nreal tickets don't split cleanly, and PMs were manually overriding ~30% of classifications\nin the first two sprints with no way to say "this is genuinely unclear, a human should\ndecide" versus "this is wrong, fix the model." This PRD adds the third bucket and the\nwritten definition backing it.	{"pm_document_id": "7bb4987e-9858-4e37-8b11-0c696165b607"}	[-0.061180774,-0.0689747,0.057459164,0.008173058,0.039573822,-0.033027317,0.028720368,-0.02197245,0.00082043605,-0.025155859,0.048246834,-0.01930912,0.015765654,0.0060687163,0.031471014,-0.0305929,0.016252477,-0.06305728,-0.020028636,0.04186148,0.092447065,-0.02909525,-0.022394925,0.019193254,0.060248513,0.056468148,0.039665114,-0.06444225,-0.05661848,-0.24353543,-0.019072529,-0.026924152,-0.029494438,0.00067159446,-0.006334726,-0.030085066,-0.046679888,0.03036631,-0.02316099,0.047669798,0.0006952625,-8.164328e-05,-0.04129046,-0.009449828,-0.008028845,-0.06010882,-0.015091782,-0.014037071,-0.024432445,-0.06553764,0.060677554,-0.030159453,-0.056787718,0.021153273,-0.02448199,0.030778991,0.028325614,0.05971017,0.043898724,0.037686773,-0.004892895,-0.01341251,-0.1166345,-0.029398238,0.043361492,0.015547478,-0.010361206,-0.09610009,-0.031857833,0.022198265,0.02412838,0.050246745,-0.027267046,0.050029032,-0.022969335,-0.031806845,0.013513213,0.03706207,0.007302277,0.019869192,0.0027873851,0.025173897,-0.029472556,-0.0036466105,0.029814815,-0.0214917,-0.014664277,-0.00048743095,0.026933968,0.043451805,0.014179184,-0.009609973,0.029207956,0.015076346,-0.07121268,0.024562532,0.04531407,-0.007456331,0.005429562,0.43548813,-0.02392823,0.022477737,-0.041157544,