db781e41-29cb-4ab6-b48d-d187254333a8	acme-data-migration-20d649	deliverables_matrix	DELIV-MATRIX-01	client	1.0	2026-09-14	A. Gupta	final	\N	f	03_deliverables_matrix.md	/Users/anyagupta/Documents/idea-explainer-pro/backend/storage/pm_documents/acme-data-migration-20d649/db781e41-29cb-4ab6-b48d-d187254333a8.md	e450dca6a7951225452d25a4301abec8c708113758c66d3f6594b3e7119bf795	confirmed	1	Front matter present and valid — deterministic parse, no LLM call.	\N	{"people": [], "cr_refs": ["CR-002"], "risk_ids": ["R-02"], "ticket_refs": ["KPD-116", "KPD-119", "KPD-146", "KPD-247"], "decision_ids": [], "deliverable_ids": ["D1", "D2", "D3", "D4", "D5", "D6", "D7", "D8"], "requirement_ids": []}	agupta	2026-09-14 17:25:43.699107+00	agupta	2026-09-14 17:27:15.852045+00	[{"content": "| ID | Deliverable | Acceptance Criteria | Due | Client Reviewer | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| D1 | Data Ingestion Connectors (Jira + GitHub) | Sync within 5 min of change; full backfill with no manual steps; webhook survives 50+ events/min bursts; non-UTF8 attachment filenames don't fail silently | 2026-04-30 | Dana Whitfield | Accepted (2026-04-24, with conditions — see UAT-D1) |", "section_path": "Deliverables Matrix > D1"}, {"content": "| ID | Deliverable | Acceptance Criteria | Due | Client Reviewer | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| D2 | Ticket-to-Commit Linkage & Coverage Reporting | Commit-message ticket refs link correctly across Arclight's conventions; coverage % updates live; no double-counting | 2026-07-20 (revised, CR-002) | Dana Whitfield | In Progress — behind original date, see R-02 |", "section_path": "Deliverables Matrix > D2"}, {"content": "| ID | Deliverable | Acceptance Criteria | Due | Client Reviewer | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| D3 | Hybrid Search & Cited Q&A | Combined keyword+semantic results; every answer cited; p95 < 2s at 200k chunks; abstains rather than fabricates | 2026-08-15 | Dana Whitfield | In Progress |", "section_path": "Deliverables Matrix > D3"}, {"content": "| ID | Deliverable | Acceptance Criteria | Due | Client Reviewer | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| D4 | Handover Brief & Work-State Assembly | Brief reflects live Jira/GitHub state; shows others' pending reviews correctly; no self-reported input required | 2026-10-31 | Marcus Feld | Not Started — acceptance criteria drafted 2026-09-11 (KPD-119), dev not yet started |", "section_path": "Deliverables Matrix > D4"}, {"content": "| ID | Deliverable | Acceptance Criteria | Due | Client Reviewer | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| D5 | Scope Guardian — SOW Parsing & Classification | Uploaded SOW produces editable deliverable list; tickets classified in/out/ambiguous with a stated, consistent reason | 2026-09-30 | Dana Whitfield | In Progress — \\"ambiguous vs out-of-scope\\" definition just landed (KPD-116, 2026-09-11) |", "section_path": "Deliverables Matrix > D5"}, {"content": "| ID | Deliverable | Acceptance Criteria | Due | Client Reviewer | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| D6 | Provenance & Read-Time Permission Evaluation | Every citation traces to source; revoked access takes effect on next query, no cache flush/restart; row-level security enforced | 2026-09-30 | Chris Okafor | In Progress — critical revocation-lag bug fixed 2026-09-11 (KPD-247), pending re-verification |", "section_path": "Deliverables Matrix > D6"}, {"content": "| ID | Deliverable | Acceptance Criteria | Due | Client Reviewer | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| D7 | Secrets Scanning & Canary Tokens | Common secret patterns caught pre-index; canary alert fires reliably even through webhook flakiness; low false-positive rate | 2026-10-31 | Chris Okafor | In Review — core scanning done, canary false-positive-on-own-seed bug fixed (KPD-146) |", "section_path": "Deliverables Matrix > D7"}, {"content": "| ID | Deliverable | Acceptance Criteria | Due | Client Reviewer | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| D8 | Auto-Draft from PRs — Assisted Capture | Draft generated per qualifying merged PR; sits pending until human approval; searchable with provenance once approved | 2026-11-30 | Marcus Feld | Not Started — scope confirmation needed, see Epic Brief EPIC-D8 and Open Question below |", "section_path": "Deliverables Matrix > D8"}]
551b3e5e-9b42-45d9-9171-e4e7ac75bff6	acme-data-migration-20d649	requirements	PRD-D5-01	internal	0.3	2026-09-08	Omar K	final	\N	f	04_prd_scope_guardian.md	/Users/anyagupta/Documents/idea-explainer-pro/backend/storage/pm_documents/acme-data-migration-20d649/551b3e5e-9b42-45d9-9171-e4e7ac75bff6.md	bd5bdb86a2953e47e856cd16fd2b6a1909d6b71c6ca188d7c59f60105fa1d42b	confirmed	1	Front matter present and valid — deterministic parse, no LLM call.	\N	{"people": [], "cr_refs": [], "risk_ids": [], "ticket_refs": ["KPD-5"], "decision_ids": [], "deliverable_ids": ["D2", "D5"], "requirement_ids": ["FR-01", "FR-02", "FR-03", "FR-04", "FR-05", "NFR-01", "NFR-02"]}	agupta	2026-09-14 17:25:43.735583+00	agupta	2026-09-14 17:27:16.144105+00	[{"content": "# PRD — Scope Guardian Classification (D5)", "section_path": "(preamble)"}, {"content": "## Objective / Summary\\nD5 classifies incoming Jira tickets as in-scope, out-of-scope, or ambiguous against the\\nparsed SOW. Original build (KPD-5 epic) shipped classification with only two buckets\\n(in-scope / out-of-scope), which PM feedback flagged almost immediately as unusable —\\nreal tickets don't split cleanly, and PMs were manually overriding ~30% of classifications\\nin the first two sprints with no way to say \\"this is genuinely unclear, a human should\\ndecide\\" versus \\"this is wrong, fix the model.\\" This PRD adds the third bucket and the\\nwritten definition backing it.", "section_path": "Objective / Summary"}, {"content": "## Background\\nManual override log (Apr–Jun 2026, n=118 classified tickets): 34 overrides, of which PM\\nnotes on 21 said some version of \\"not wrong, just not clearly D-anything.\\" Zero written\\ndefinition existed for what should count as ambiguous versus wrong — the classifier prompt\\njust said \\"classify as in-scope or out-of-scope,\\" so real ambiguity was being forced into\\none bucket or the other and undermining trust in the flag generally (Dana Whitfield raised\\nthis directly in the 2026-08-14 client sync — see Meeting Notes archive from that date).", "section_path": "Background"}, {"content": "## Goals & Non-Goals\\n**Goals:** third classification bucket (\\"ambiguous\\"); a written, testable definition of\\nambiguous vs. out-of-scope; classification reason is always shown, not just the label.\\n**Non-Goals:** auto-closing or auto-transitioning any ticket based on classification\\n(SOW D5 exclusion — PM review only); legal redlining of the SOW itself; retroactively\\nreclassifying already-PM-reviewed tickets from before this change.", "section_path": "Goals & Non-Goals"}, {"content": "## Functional Requirements\\n- FR-01: Classifier output includes one of {in_scope, out_of_scope, ambiguous} plus a\\n  free-text reason string, always populated (never blank).\\n- FR-02: \\"Ambiguous\\" applies when the ticket's stated work matches a SOW deliverable's\\n  *title/theme* but not its acceptance criteria or explicitly touches an EXCLUDES line\\n  without being clearly performing the excluded action itself (e.g., a ticket about\\n  \\"improving handover brief accuracy\\" that turns out to touch scoring language should be\\n  flagged ambiguous, not silently classified either way).\\n- FR-03: \\"Out-of-scope\\" applies only when the ticket's work matches no deliverable AND/OR\\n  directly performs something on an EXCLUDES list.\\n- FR-04: PM override of any classification is logged with an optional reason, feeding a\\n  monthly precision review (not built yet — tracked as FR-05 for a later revision).\\n- FR-05 (v2, not this PRD): monthly override-rate dashboard per classification bucket.", "section_path": "Functional Requirements"}, {"content": "## Non-Functional Requirements\\n- NFR-01: Classification reason must be under 200 characters, no jargon the PM would need\\n  to look up (readable by a non-engineer PM).\\n- NFR-02: Re-classification of an existing ticket on SOW update must complete for the full\\n  backlog within 10 minutes (this SOW has ~250 tickets; future clients may have more).", "section_path": "Non-Functional Requirements"}, {"content": "## Rollout Plan\\nShip behind a flag scoped to Arclight only first (this is the only live engagement).\\nBackfill-reclassify the current backlog once FR-01–03 land; do NOT reclassify anything a\\nPM has already manually reviewed (would silently overwrite a human judgment call).", "section_path": "Rollout Plan"}, {"content": "## Success Metrics\\nOverride rate on \\"ambiguous\\"-labeled tickets drops below 15% within one sprint of rollout\\n(vs. the current ~29% effective override rate hiding inside the binary classifier).", "section_path": "Success Metrics"}, {"content": "## Open Questions\\n- OQ-01: Should \\"ambiguous\\" tickets block a coverage-report percentage the way out-of-scope\\n  ones do, or count separately? Decision deadline: 2026-09-18 (before D2's coverage-report\\n  work depends on a stable answer). Owner: A. Gupta + Dana Whitfield.", "section_path": "Open Questions"}]
53a90022-6bd7-4982-8502-d7dadf5f826e	acme-data-migration-20d649	change_request	CR-002	client	1.0	2026-06-09	A. Gupta	final	\N	f	05_change_request_cr002.md	/Users/anyagupta/Documents/idea-explainer-pro/backend/storage/pm_documents/acme-data-migration-20d649/53a90022-6bd7-4982-8502-d7dadf5f826e.md	1bd14724c5c46c71f06e05ad30baf1302f259ee12812801aecc91c5c09a4e080	confirmed	1	Front matter present and valid — deterministic parse, no LLM call.	\N	{"people": [], "cr_refs": ["CR-002", "CR-003"], "risk_ids": ["R-02"], "ticket_refs": ["KPD-115", "KPD-123", "KPD-136", "KPD-146"], "decision_ids": [], "deliverable_ids": ["D2", "D3", "D5", "D6", "D7"], "requirement_ids": []}	agupta	2026-09-14 17:25:43.772539+00	agupta	2026-09-14 17:27:16.522178+00	[{"content": "# Change Request CR-002 — D2 Milestone Date Revision", "section_path": "(preamble)"}, {"content": "## Description\\nD2 (Ticket-to-Commit Linkage & Coverage Reporting) was contracted for acceptance by\\n2026-06-15. Requesting the date move to **2026-07-20**. No change to D2's acceptance\\ncriteria or fee — this is a schedule-only request.", "section_path": "Description"}, {"content": "## Business Reason\\nTwo compounding causes, surfaced across KPD-115, KPD-123, and KPD-136:\\n1. The linkage matcher underestimated how many of Arclight's historical commit-message\\n   conventions needed handling (parenthetical ticket refs, refs buried mid-message, refs\\n   split across a commit + its PR title rather than in the commit itself) — three extra\\n   convention patterns found during real-corpus testing that weren't in the original\\n   sample Arclight provided at kickoff.\\n2. Retrieval team velocity ran under plan in Sprints 5–6 (Priya Kumar and Shubhr Aryan\\n   were pulled ~30% onto a D3 spike to unblock D7's secrets-scanning integration, which\\n   was originally scheduled after D2 but got reprioritized when a false-positive canary\\n   issue (KPD-146 class of bug) risked contaminating the eval harness for every other\\n   deliverable being tested against it).", "section_path": "Business Reason"}, {"content": "## Impact Assessment\\n- **Effort:** +8 points against the original D2 estimate (convention handling was\\n  under-scoped, not newly invented work).\\n- **Schedule impact:** D2 acceptance moves 2026-06-15 → 2026-07-20 (5 weeks). Does not\\n  cascade to D3/D5/D6 target dates — those tracks are staffed independently.\\n- **Cost impact:** None. Fixed-fee deliverable; the extra effort is absorbed, not billed.", "section_path": "Impact Assessment"}, {"content": "## Recommendation\\nApprove the date move. The alternative — holding the original date — would mean shipping\\nD2 with known gaps in linkage coverage for at least 3 real commit-message patterns Arclight\\nactually uses, which undermines the whole point of the coverage-report metric.", "section_path": "Recommendation"}, {"content": "## Disposition\\n**Approved.** Dana Whitfield (Arclight, client reviewer) and Marcus Feld (sponsor) signed\\noff via email 2026-06-09. New target: 2026-07-20. Deliverables Matrix and Charter updated\\nto reflect the revised date; Risk & Issue Log entry R-02 tracks progress against it.\\n\\nNote (added 2026-08-02, A. Gupta): D2 did not close by the revised date either — as of this\\nwriting it's still In Progress. See R-02 in the risk log for current status rather than\\ntreating this CR's date as authoritative; a second date revision has been discussed\\ninformally with Dana but not yet formalized as CR-003. If it slips again past September,\\nraise CR-003 properly instead of letting the matrix date go stale.", "section_path": "Disposition"}]
08cae025-e66c-4b19-bd00-ac5fab9c84b0	acme-data-migration-20d649	epic_brief	EPIC-D8	client	0.2	2026-09-08	A. Gupta	draft	\N	f	06_epic_brief_d8.md	/Users/anyagupta/Documents/idea-explainer-pro/backend/storage/pm_documents/acme-data-migration-20d649/08cae025-e66c-4b19-bd00-ac5fab9c84b0.md	5ba1084d4799c5b5fd40d868fc5b59105cf39125a495c446034684faa2277153	confirmed	1	Front matter present and valid — deterministic parse, no LLM call.	\N	{"people": [], "cr_refs": [], "risk_ids": ["R-03"], "ticket_refs": [], "decision_ids": [], "deliverable_ids": ["D3", "D8"], "requirement_ids": []}	agupta	2026-09-14 17:25:43.805553+00	agupta	2026-09-14 17:27:16.751517+00	[{"content": "# Epic Brief — D8: Auto-Draft from PRs (Assisted Capture)\\n\\n> Status: pre-kickoff draft. Not yet started — see Open Questions before committing a\\n> sprint to this. Client reviewer: Marcus Feld.", "section_path": "(preamble)"}, {"content": "## Problem Statement\\nMerged PRs carry reasoning (why this approach, what was tried and rejected, what to watch\\nfor later) that currently lives only in the PR thread and evaporates from team memory once\\nthe thread scrolls off anyone's radar. Success measure: ≥70% of qualifying merged PRs get\\nan approved draft note within 48 hours of merge, measured over the first month post-launch.", "section_path": "Problem Statement"}, {"content": "## Scope\\n**In:** auto-generate a draft knowledge-base note per qualifying merged PR (summary + reasoning\\nextracted from the PR description and commit messages); human-approval gate before publish;\\nsearchable via D3 once approved, with provenance back to the source PR.\\n**Out (per SOW D8 exclusions):** auto-publish without approval; PRs/repos outside Arclight's\\nconnected GitHub org; translation to non-English.", "section_path": "Scope"}, {"content": "## Technical Approach\\nExtract PR description + linked ticket + commit messages → LLM summarization pass →\\npending-review row → PM/eng-lead approval UI → on approval, chunk + embed + index through\\nthe same pipeline D3 already uses, tagged `doc_type: auto_draft_note`.", "section_path": "Technical Approach"}, {"content": "## Story Breakdown\\n| Story ID | Title | Est. pts |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| KPD-TBD-1 | PR metadata extraction + summarization prompt | 5 |\\n| KPD-TBD-2 | Pending-review queue + approval UI | 8 |\\n| KPD-TBD-3 | Approved-note indexing into D3's search | 3 |\\n| KPD-TBD-4 | Provenance linking back to source PR | 3 |\\n\\n(Ticket numbers not yet cut in Jira — pending the scope question below. Don't cut them\\nearly and then have to re-scope mid-sprint if the answer changes what \\"qualifying\\" means.)", "section_path": "Story Breakdown"}, {"content": "## Dependencies\\n| Item | Owner | Due |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| D3 indexing pipeline stable enough to extend | Relay (Jason Maro) | Already met |\\n| Confirmation of \\"qualifying PR\\" definition | Dana Whitfield (client) | See Open Questions |", "section_path": "Dependencies"}, {"content": "## Open Questions\\n- OQ-01: Does \\"assisted capture\\" include drafting from long PR **comment threads**\\n  post-merge, not just the diff + description? Raised informally by client (Slack via Dana,\\n  2026-09-03). Materially changes story-point estimate (comment-thread extraction is a\\n  different, harder extraction problem than PR description parsing). **Decision deadline:\\n  2026-09-19** — if unresolved, this epic does not start on schedule and D8's Nov 30 date\\n  is at risk. Owner: A. Gupta + Dana Whitfield. If the answer expands scope, this needs a\\n  formal CR, not just an epic-brief footnote.", "section_path": "Open Questions"}, {"content": "## Risks\\nSee R-03 in the Risk & Issue Log (scope ambiguity, same underlying question as OQ-01).", "section_path": "Risks"}, {"content": "## Estimate & Timeline\\n19 points as scoped today (excludes comment-thread extraction). Earliest start: once OQ-01\\nresolves. At current team velocity (~24 pts/sprint across the whole team, not just this\\nepic), this fits in one sprint once unblocked — the risk is entirely the open question, not\\nthe build.", "section_path": "Estimate & Timeline"}]
60e8e68b-2f3c-40ae-8ecc-55ac1e0a5814	acme-data-migration-20d649	sprint_planning	\N	internal	1.0	2026-09-14	A. Gupta	final	2026-09-15	f	07_sprint_planning_sprint14.md	/Users/anyagupta/Documents/idea-explainer-pro/backend/storage/pm_documents/acme-data-migration-20d649/60e8e68b-2f3c-40ae-8ecc-55ac1e0a5814.md	0fb8fb24898c775881da823962482ac496c9fbb70dff96918c614ef607087a75	confirmed	1	Front matter present and valid — deterministic parse, no LLM call.	\N	{"people": [], "cr_refs": ["CR-002"], "risk_ids": ["R-01"], "ticket_refs": ["KPD-101", "KPD-11", "KPD-127", "KPD-133", "KPD-247"], "decision_ids": [], "deliverable_ids": ["D2", "D3", "D5", "D6", "D8"], "requirement_ids": []}	agupta	2026-09-14 17:25:43.840198+00	agupta	2026-09-14 17:27:16.978935+00	[{"content": "# Sprint 14 Planning Notes", "section_path": "(preamble)"}, {"content": "## Header\\nSprint 14 · 2026-09-15 → 2026-09-26 · Planning held 2026-09-14\\nAttendees: A. Gupta, Akshar Kher, Jason Maro, Omar K, Priya Kumar, Shubhr Aryan\\nAbsent: Agrim Gairola (personal leave, started 2026-09-08, expected back ~2026-09-29 —\\nsee R-01 in risk log; his in-flight D5/D3-adjacent tickets were reassigned, not deferred,\\nper the note below)\\nCapacity: 5 of 6 engineers available (Agrim out) → capacity calc 32 pts (down from usual\\n~40; not fully reduced 1/6 since two of his tickets were already near-done and just needed\\nsomeone else to finish, not restart)\\nCommitted velocity target: 30 pts (leaving buffer given last sprint ran over — see Sprint 13\\nretro, \\"what went poorly\\")", "section_path": "Header"}, {"content": "## Sprint Backlog\\n| Story ID | Title | Pts |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| KPD-127 | SOW deliverable mapping for D3 out of date after classifier rewrite | 3 |\\n| KPD-133 | Written definition of ambiguous vs out-of-scope — remaining edge cases | 2 |\\n| KPD-101 | Ask endpoint returns 500 instead of 429 when downstream rate limit hit | 3 |\\n| KPD-11 | Comment ingestion truncates bodies over 32KB instead of paginating | 5 |\\n| — | D6 revocation-lag fix (KPD-247) re-verification against full regression suite | 5 |\\n| — | D2 linkage: pick up remaining commit-convention edge cases post-CR-002 | 8 |\\n| — | D8 epic: blocked pending OQ-01 (see Epic Brief EPIC-D8) — not pulled into backlog | 0 |\\n\\nTotal: 26 pts pulled against a 30 pt target — deliberately left ~4 pts of slack given the\\nAgrim gap and because KPD-127 (reassigned from Agrim) may take longer for someone unfamiliar\\nwith that code path to pick up cleanly.", "section_path": "Sprint Backlog"}, {"content": "## Dependencies Pulled In\\n- Dana Whitfield's answer on OQ-01 (D8 scope) — needed by 2026-09-19 per the epic brief;\\n  not a blocker for this sprint's committed work, but flagged so nobody quietly starts D8\\n  prep work before it resolves.", "section_path": "Dependencies Pulled In"}, {"content": "## Definition of Done\\nStandard project DoD applies (stored once in project config, not restated per sprint) — code\\nreviewed, tests passing, deployed to staging, ticket linked to its commit for D2 coverage\\npurposes(!), acceptance criteria checked off by the ticket owner before moving to Done.", "section_path": "Definition of Done"}]
dffe989a-2626-405e-b3c0-06688bbf4932	acme-data-migration-20d649	sprint_review	\N	internal	1.0	2026-09-12	A. Gupta	final	2026-09-01	f	08_sprint_review_sprint13.md	/Users/anyagupta/Documents/idea-explainer-pro/backend/storage/pm_documents/acme-data-migration-20d649/dffe989a-2626-405e-b3c0-06688bbf4932.md	0e0f2bf928dcfd2b22475f77136064c6aecb5973c27fa439349744cdf849d2ea	confirmed	1	Front matter present and valid — deterministic parse, no LLM call.	\N	{"people": [], "cr_refs": ["CR-002"], "risk_ids": ["R-02"], "ticket_refs": ["KPD-115", "KPD-116", "KPD-119", "KPD-247"], "decision_ids": [], "deliverable_ids": ["D1", "D2", "D4", "D5", "D6"], "requirement_ids": []}	agupta	2026-09-14 17:25:43.874307+00	agupta	2026-09-14 17:27:17.19761+00	[{"content": "# Sprint 13 Review Notes", "section_path": "(preamble)"}, {"content": "## Header\\nSprint 13 · 2026-09-01 → 2026-09-11 · Review held 2026-09-12\\nAudience: internal team + Dana Whitfield (partial, first 20 min)", "section_path": "Header"}, {"content": "## Demonstrated\\n- KPD-247 (D6): read-time permission evaluation now correctly revokes access on next query\\n  without a cache flush/restart — the core D6 acceptance bar. Demoed a live revoke against\\n  a staging user. **Accepted internally**, pending Chris Okafor's security sign-off before\\n  it counts toward D6's client acceptance.\\n- KPD-119 (D4): acceptance criteria written and reviewed — no code yet, this was intentionally\\n  a spec-first ticket ahead of D4 dev starting. **Not a demo-able item**, included for\\n  visibility since a PM asked \\"what happened with D4 this sprint.\\"\\n- KPD-116 (D5): three-bucket classifier (in/out/ambiguous) shipped with the written\\n  definition from the PRD. Demoed against 6 previously-overridden tickets from the manual\\n  override log — 5 of 6 now classify correctly without override. **Accepted internally.**", "section_path": "Demonstrated"}, {"content": "## Feedback & Requests\\n- Dana (during her 20 min): asked why D2's coverage number still looked lower than expected\\n  given CR-002 was supposed to have fixed the convention-matching gap. Mapped to KPD-115/123\\n  — those are still in progress, CR-002 approved the *date*, not a claim that the work was\\n  already done by that date. Logged as a communication gap to fix, not a technical one — see\\n  retro.\\n- Parking lot: Dana asked if the classifier's \\"ambiguous\\" reason text could be exposed to\\n  her team directly rather than only to the internal PM view. Not scoped in D5's SOW acceptance\\n  criteria as written; noted for a possible CR if she wants to pursue it, not committed to.", "section_path": "Feedback & Requests"}, {"content": "## Metrics Update\\nVelocity: 24 pts completed against a 28 pt commitment (86%) — third sprint in a row under\\ncommitment; see retro action items. Milestone health: D1 accepted, D5/D6 tracking to\\n2026-09-30, D2 still amber (see Deliverables Matrix and R-02).", "section_path": "Metrics Update"}]
