57dc50dc-d3b1-40b7-b3e2-9b6b5045472c	acme-data-migration-20d649	charter	CHARTER-01	internal	1.2	2026-03-01	A. Gupta	final	\N	t	02_project_charter.md	/Users/anyagupta/Documents/idea-explainer-pro/backend/storage/pm_documents/acme-data-migration-20d649/57dc50dc-d3b1-40b7-b3e2-9b6b5045472c.md	af1e66c4ad2d9f558b98366b2743683fcae25983dd8fd86e042a126776e238db	confirmed	1	Front matter present and valid — deterministic parse, no LLM call.	\N	{"people": [], "cr_refs": ["CR-002"], "risk_ids": ["R-01", "R-02", "R-03", "R-04"], "ticket_refs": [], "decision_ids": [], "deliverable_ids": ["D1", "D2", "D3", "D4", "D5", "D6", "D7", "D8"], "requirement_ids": []}	agupta	2026-09-14 17:25:55.541674+00	agupta	2026-09-14 17:30:37.433209+00	[{"content": "# Project Charter — Arclight Continuity", "section_path": "(preamble)"}, {"content": "## Problem\\nArclight's engineering org has ~40 engineers across 3 teams and no single place to answer\\n\\"what's the state of X\\" without pinging someone directly. Manager survey (n=14, Feb 2026):\\nmedian time to reconstruct a departing engineer's handover notes is **6.5 hours**, and 9/14\\nmanagers said they'd shipped a regression in the last quarter caused by missing context from\\na rotation. Support/PM Slack channel logged 61 \\"does anyone know why we did X\\" threads in\\nJanuary alone.", "section_path": "Problem"}, {"content": "## Goal\\nShip a queryable, cited knowledge layer over Jira + GitHub, with automated handover briefs,\\nby **2026-11-30** (contract end date) — target: median handover reconstruction time under\\n**45 minutes**, measured via a follow-up manager survey at UAT.", "section_path": "Goal"}, {"content": "## Non-Goals\\n- Not a replacement for Jira/GitHub — read-only layer on top of both.\\n- Not a performance/productivity tracker. Explicitly out of scope per SOW §2 (D4 exclusions).\\n- Not a compliance certification project (SOC 2 etc. is a separate, non-contracted effort).", "section_path": "Non-Goals"}, {"content": "## Ownership\\n- **Sponsor:** Marcus Feld, VP Engineering, Arclight Systems\\n- **DRI (Relay Labs):** Anya Gupta, Delivery Lead\\n- **Client reviewer:** Dana Whitfield, Program Manager, Arclight Systems\\n- **Team (Relay Labs, 6 eng + 1 lead):** A. Gupta (lead), Akshar Kher, Agrim Gairola,\\n  Jason Maro, Omar K, Priya Kumar, Shubhr Aryan — allocation: lead 0.5 FTE, engineers ~0.8\\n  FTE each against this engagement (remainder split across other client work — see Risk R-04\\n  in the risk log for what this costs us when someone's out).", "section_path": "Ownership"}, {"content": "## Budget\\nFixed fee, $214,000 total. 15% ($32,100) due at signing, remainder invoiced per-deliverable\\non UAT acceptance (see Deliverables Matrix for the D1–D8 split). See SOW §5 for the full rate\\ncard used if any deliverable goes to T&M.", "section_path": "Budget"}, {"content": "## Success Metrics\\n- Handover reconstruction time: 6.5 hrs → under 45 min (manager survey, post-UAT)\\n- Ticket-to-commit coverage (D2): ≥85% of Done/In-Progress tickets linked to a commit\\n- Retrieval p95 latency (D3): under 2s at 200k indexed chunks\\n- Zero unremediated secret leaks reaching the searchable index (D7)", "section_path": "Success Metrics"}, {"content": "## Milestones\\n| Milestone | Target Date | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Kickoff | 2026-03-02 | Done |\\n| D1 accepted (ingestion live) | 2026-04-30 | Done — accepted 2026-04-24, see UAT-D1 |\\n| D2 accepted (linkage/coverage) | 2026-06-15 | **At risk — see CR-002**, revised target 2026-07-20 |\\n| D3 accepted (hybrid search) | 2026-08-15 | In progress |\\n| D5/D6 accepted (scope + permissions) | 2026-09-30 | In progress |\\n| D4/D7 accepted | 2026-10-31 | In progress / near-done |\\n| D8 accepted, engagement close | 2026-11-30 | Not started — scope confirmation pending |", "section_path": "Milestones"}, {"content": "## Top Risks\\nFull detail lives in the Risk & Issue Log, not restated here (single-writer rule). Currently\\ntracking: R-01 (key-person coverage gap), R-02 (D2 schedule slip), R-03 (D8 scope ambiguity).", "section_path": "Top Risks"}]
921c9340-3926-432f-b6a7-b3e395bc9ea8	acme-data-migration-20d649	deliverables_matrix	DELIV-MATRIX-01	client	1.0	2026-09-14	A. Gupta	final	\N	t	03_deliverables_matrix.md	/Users/anyagupta/Documents/idea-explainer-pro/backend/storage/pm_documents/acme-data-migration-20d649/921c9340-3926-432f-b6a7-b3e395bc9ea8.md	e450dca6a7951225452d25a4301abec8c708113758c66d3f6594b3e7119bf795	confirmed	1	Front matter present and valid — deterministic parse, no LLM call.	\N	{"people": [], "cr_refs": ["CR-002"], "risk_ids": ["R-02"], "ticket_refs": ["KPD-116", "KPD-119", "KPD-146", "KPD-247"], "decision_ids": [], "deliverable_ids": ["D1", "D2", "D3", "D4", "D5", "D6", "D7", "D8"], "requirement_ids": []}	agupta	2026-09-14 17:26:16.006092+00	agupta	2026-09-14 17:30:37.91217+00	[{"content": "| ID | Deliverable | Acceptance Criteria | Due | Client Reviewer | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| D1 | Data Ingestion Connectors (Jira + GitHub) | Sync within 5 min of change; full backfill with no manual steps; webhook survives 50+ events/min bursts; non-UTF8 attachment filenames don't fail silently | 2026-04-30 | Dana Whitfield | Accepted (2026-04-24, with conditions — see UAT-D1) |", "section_path": "Deliverables Matrix > D1"}, {"content": "| ID | Deliverable | Acceptance Criteria | Due | Client Reviewer | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| D2 | Ticket-to-Commit Linkage & Coverage Reporting | Commit-message ticket refs link correctly across Arclight's conventions; coverage % updates live; no double-counting | 2026-07-20 (revised, CR-002) | Dana Whitfield | In Progress — behind original date, see R-02 |", "section_path": "Deliverables Matrix > D2"}, {"content": "| ID | Deliverable | Acceptance Criteria | Due | Client Reviewer | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| D3 | Hybrid Search & Cited Q&A | Combined keyword+semantic results; every answer cited; p95 < 2s at 200k chunks; abstains rather than fabricates | 2026-08-15 | Dana Whitfield | In Progress |", "section_path": "Deliverables Matrix > D3"}, {"content": "| ID | Deliverable | Acceptance Criteria | Due | Client Reviewer | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| D4 | Handover Brief & Work-State Assembly | Brief reflects live Jira/GitHub state; shows others' pending reviews correctly; no self-reported input required | 2026-10-31 | Marcus Feld | Not Started — acceptance criteria drafted 2026-09-11 (KPD-119), dev not yet started |", "section_path": "Deliverables Matrix > D4"}, {"content": "| ID | Deliverable | Acceptance Criteria | Due | Client Reviewer | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| D5 | Scope Guardian — SOW Parsing & Classification | Uploaded SOW produces editable deliverable list; tickets classified in/out/ambiguous with a stated, consistent reason | 2026-09-30 | Dana Whitfield | In Progress — \\"ambiguous vs out-of-scope\\" definition just landed (KPD-116, 2026-09-11) |", "section_path": "Deliverables Matrix > D5"}, {"content": "| ID | Deliverable | Acceptance Criteria | Due | Client Reviewer | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| D6 | Provenance & Read-Time Permission Evaluation | Every citation traces to source; revoked access takes effect on next query, no cache flush/restart; row-level security enforced | 2026-09-30 | Chris Okafor | In Progress — critical revocation-lag bug fixed 2026-09-11 (KPD-247), pending re-verification |", "section_path": "Deliverables Matrix > D6"}, {"content": "| ID | Deliverable | Acceptance Criteria | Due | Client Reviewer | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| D7 | Secrets Scanning & Canary Tokens | Common secret patterns caught pre-index; canary alert fires reliably even through webhook flakiness; low false-positive rate | 2026-10-31 | Chris Okafor | In Review — core scanning done, canary false-positive-on-own-seed bug fixed (KPD-146) |", "section_path": "Deliverables Matrix > D7"}, {"content": "| ID | Deliverable | Acceptance Criteria | Due | Client Reviewer | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| D8 | Auto-Draft from PRs — Assisted Capture | Draft generated per qualifying merged PR; sits pending until human approval; searchable with provenance once approved | 2026-11-30 | Marcus Feld | Not Started — scope confirmation needed, see Epic Brief EPIC-D8 and Open Question below |", "section_path": "Deliverables Matrix > D8"}]
7bb4987e-9858-4e37-8b11-0c696165b607	acme-data-migration-20d649	requirements	PRD-D5-01	internal	0.3	2026-09-08	Omar K	final	\N	t	04_prd_scope_guardian.md	/Users/anyagupta/Documents/idea-explainer-pro/backend/storage/pm_documents/acme-data-migration-20d649/7bb4987e-9858-4e37-8b11-0c696165b607.md	bd5bdb86a2953e47e856cd16fd2b6a1909d6b71c6ca188d7c59f60105fa1d42b	confirmed	1	Front matter present and valid — deterministic parse, no LLM call.	\N	{"people": [], "cr_refs": [], "risk_ids": [], "ticket_refs": ["KPD-5"], "decision_ids": [], "deliverable_ids": ["D2", "D5"], "requirement_ids": ["FR-01", "FR-02", "FR-03", "FR-04", "FR-05", "NFR-01", "NFR-02"]}	agupta	2026-09-14 17:26:16.056057+00	agupta	2026-09-14 17:30:38.152647+00	[{"content": "# PRD — Scope Guardian Classification (D5)", "section_path": "(preamble)"}, {"content": "## Objective / Summary\\nD5 classifies incoming Jira tickets as in-scope, out-of-scope, or ambiguous against the\\nparsed SOW. Original build (KPD-5 epic) shipped classification with only two buckets\\n(in-scope / out-of-scope), which PM feedback flagged almost immediately as unusable —\\nreal tickets don't split cleanly, and PMs were manually overriding ~30% of classifications\\nin the first two sprints with no way to say \\"this is genuinely unclear, a human should\\ndecide\\" versus \\"this is wrong, fix the model.\\" This PRD adds the third bucket and the\\nwritten definition backing it.", "section_path": "Objective / Summary"}, {"content": "## Background\\nManual override log (Apr–Jun 2026, n=118 classified tickets): 34 overrides, of which PM\\nnotes on 21 said some version of \\"not wrong, just not clearly D-anything.\\" Zero written\\ndefinition existed for what should count as ambiguous versus wrong — the classifier prompt\\njust said \\"classify as in-scope or out-of-scope,\\" so real ambiguity was being forced into\\none bucket or the other and undermining trust in the flag generally (Dana Whitfield raised\\nthis directly in the 2026-08-14 client sync — see Meeting Notes archive from that date).", "section_path": "Background"}, {"content": "## Goals & Non-Goals\\n**Goals:** third classification bucket (\\"ambiguous\\"); a written, testable definition of\\nambiguous vs. out-of-scope; classification reason is always shown, not just the label.\\n**Non-Goals:** auto-closing or auto-transitioning any ticket based on classification\\n(SOW D5 exclusion — PM review only); legal redlining of the SOW itself; retroactively\\nreclassifying already-PM-reviewed tickets from before this change.", "section_path": "Goals & Non-Goals"}, {"content": "## Functional Requirements\\n- FR-01: Classifier output includes one of {in_scope, out_of_scope, ambiguous} plus a\\n  free-text reason string, always populated (never blank).\\n- FR-02: \\"Ambiguous\\" applies when the ticket's stated work matches a SOW deliverable's\\n  *title/theme* but not its acceptance criteria or explicitly touches an EXCLUDES line\\n  without being clearly performing the excluded action itself (e.g., a ticket about\\n  \\"improving handover brief accuracy\\" that turns out to touch scoring language should be\\n  flagged ambiguous, not silently classified either way).\\n- FR-03: \\"Out-of-scope\\" applies only when the ticket's work matches no deliverable AND/OR\\n  directly performs something on an EXCLUDES list.\\n- FR-04: PM override of any classification is logged with an optional reason, feeding a\\n  monthly precision review (not built yet — tracked as FR-05 for a later revision).\\n- FR-05 (v2, not this PRD): monthly override-rate dashboard per classification bucket.", "section_path": "Functional Requirements"}, {"content": "## Non-Functional Requirements\\n- NFR-01: Classification reason must be under 200 characters, no jargon the PM would need\\n  to look up (readable by a non-engineer PM).\\n- NFR-02: Re-classification of an existing ticket on SOW update must complete for the full\\n  backlog within 10 minutes (this SOW has ~250 tickets; future clients may have more).", "section_path": "Non-Functional Requirements"}, {"content": "## Rollout Plan\\nShip behind a flag scoped to Arclight only first (this is the only live engagement).\\nBackfill-reclassify the current backlog once FR-01–03 land; do NOT reclassify anything a\\nPM has already manually reviewed (would silently overwrite a human judgment call).", "section_path": "Rollout Plan"}, {"content": "## Success Metrics\\nOverride rate on \\"ambiguous\\"-labeled tickets drops below 15% within one sprint of rollout\\n(vs. the current ~29% effective override rate hiding inside the binary classifier).", "section_path": "Success Metrics"}, {"content": "## Open Questions\\n- OQ-01: Should \\"ambiguous\\" tickets block a coverage-report percentage the way out-of-scope\\n  ones do, or count separately? Decision deadline: 2026-09-18 (before D2's coverage-report\\n  work depends on a stable answer). Owner: A. Gupta + Dana Whitfield.", "section_path": "Open Questions"}]
35bf25ea-3c20-4652-bc94-aa21b12bbb48	acme-data-migration-20d649	change_request	CR-002	client	1.0	2026-06-09	A. Gupta	final	\N	t	05_change_request_cr002.md	/Users/anyagupta/Documents/idea-explainer-pro/backend/storage/pm_documents/acme-data-migration-20d649/35bf25ea-3c20-4652-bc94-aa21b12bbb48.md	1bd14724c5c46c71f06e05ad30baf1302f259ee12812801aecc91c5c09a4e080	confirmed	1	Front matter present and valid — deterministic parse, no LLM call.	\N	{"people": [], "cr_refs": ["CR-002", "CR-003"], "risk_ids": ["R-02"], "ticket_refs": ["KPD-115", "KPD-123", "KPD-136", "KPD-146"], "decision_ids": [], "deliverable_ids": ["D2", "D3", "D5", "D6", "D7"], "requirement_ids": []}	agupta	2026-09-14 17:26:16.093606+00	agupta	2026-09-14 17:30:38.458181+00	[{"content": "# Change Request CR-002 — D2 Milestone Date Revision", "section_path": "(preamble)"}, {"content": "## Description\\nD2 (Ticket-to-Commit Linkage & Coverage Reporting) was contracted for acceptance by\\n2026-06-15. Requesting the date move to **2026-07-20**. No change to D2's acceptance\\ncriteria or fee — this is a schedule-only request.", "section_path": "Description"}, {"content": "## Business Reason\\nTwo compounding causes, surfaced across KPD-115, KPD-123, and KPD-136:\\n1. The linkage matcher underestimated how many of Arclight's historical commit-message\\n   conventions needed handling (parenthetical ticket refs, refs buried mid-message, refs\\n   split across a commit + its PR title rather than in the commit itself) — three extra\\n   convention patterns found during real-corpus testing that weren't in the original\\n   sample Arclight provided at kickoff.\\n2. Retrieval team velocity ran under plan in Sprints 5–6 (Priya Kumar and Shubhr Aryan\\n   were pulled ~30% onto a D3 spike to unblock D7's secrets-scanning integration, which\\n   was originally scheduled after D2 but got reprioritized when a false-positive canary\\n   issue (KPD-146 class of bug) risked contaminating the eval harness for every other\\n   deliverable being tested against it).", "section_path": "Business Reason"}, {"content": "## Impact Assessment\\n- **Effort:** +8 points against the original D2 estimate (convention handling was\\n  under-scoped, not newly invented work).\\n- **Schedule impact:** D2 acceptance moves 2026-06-15 → 2026-07-20 (5 weeks). Does not\\n  cascade to D3/D5/D6 target dates — those tracks are staffed independently.\\n- **Cost impact:** None. Fixed-fee deliverable; the extra effort is absorbed, not billed.", "section_path": "Impact Assessment"}, {"content": "## Recommendation\\nApprove the date move. The alternative — holding the original date — would mean shipping\\nD2 with known gaps in linkage coverage for at least 3 real commit-message patterns Arclight\\nactually uses, which undermines the whole point of the coverage-report metric.", "section_path": "Recommendation"}, {"content": "## Disposition\\n**Approved.** Dana Whitfield (Arclight, client reviewer) and Marcus Feld (sponsor) signed\\noff via email 2026-06-09. New target: 2026-07-20. Deliverables Matrix and Charter updated\\nto reflect the revised date; Risk & Issue Log entry R-02 tracks progress against it.\\n\\nNote (added 2026-08-02, A. Gupta): D2 did not close by the revised date either — as of this\\nwriting it's still In Progress. See R-02 in the risk log for current status rather than\\ntreating this CR's date as authoritative; a second date revision has been discussed\\ninformally with Dana but not yet formalized as CR-003. If it slips again past September,\\nraise CR-003 properly instead of letting the matrix date go stale.", "section_path": "Disposition"}]
13c20137-70a2-4209-b6d6-dddf294b3e7c	acme-data-migration-20d649	epic_brief	EPIC-D8	client	0.2	2026-09-08	A. Gupta	draft	\N	t	06_epic_brief_d8.md	/Users/anyagupta/Documents/idea-explainer-pro/backend/storage/pm_documents/acme-data-migration-20d649/13c20137-70a2-4209-b6d6-dddf294b3e7c.md	5ba1084d4799c5b5fd40d868fc5b59105cf39125a495c446034684faa2277153	confirmed	1	Front matter present and valid — deterministic parse, no LLM call.	\N	{"people": [], "cr_refs": [], "risk_ids": ["R-03"], "ticket_refs": [], "decision_ids": [], "deliverable_ids": ["D3", "D8"], "requirement_ids": []}	agupta	2026-09-14 17:26:16.127938+00	agupta	2026-09-14 17:30:38.675795+00	[{"content": "# Epic Brief — D8: Auto-Draft from PRs (Assisted Capture)\\n\\n> Status: pre-kickoff draft. Not yet started — see Open Questions before committing a\\n> sprint to this. Client reviewer: Marcus Feld.", "section_path": "(preamble)"}, {"content": "## Problem Statement\\nMerged PRs carry reasoning (why this approach, what was tried and rejected, what to watch\\nfor later) that currently lives only in the PR thread and evaporates from team memory once\\nthe thread scrolls off anyone's radar. Success measure: ≥70% of qualifying merged PRs get\\nan approved draft note within 48 hours of merge, measured over the first month post-launch.", "section_path": "Problem Statement"}, {"content": "## Scope\\n**In:** auto-generate a draft knowledge-base note per qualifying merged PR (summary + reasoning\\nextracted from the PR description and commit messages); human-approval gate before publish;\\nsearchable via D3 once approved, with provenance back to the source PR.\\n**Out (per SOW D8 exclusions):** auto-publish without approval; PRs/repos outside Arclight's\\nconnected GitHub org; translation to non-English.", "section_path": "Scope"}, {"content": "## Technical Approach\\nExtract PR description + linked ticket + commit messages → LLM summarization pass →\\npending-review row → PM/eng-lead approval UI → on approval, chunk + embed + index through\\nthe same pipeline D3 already uses, tagged `doc_type: auto_draft_note`.", "section_path": "Technical Approach"}, {"content": "## Story Breakdown\\n| Story ID | Title | Est. pts |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| KPD-TBD-1 | PR metadata extraction + summarization prompt | 5 |\\n| KPD-TBD-2 | Pending-review queue + approval UI | 8 |\\n| KPD-TBD-3 | Approved-note indexing into D3's search | 3 |\\n| KPD-TBD-4 | Provenance linking back to source PR | 3 |\\n\\n(Ticket numbers not yet cut in Jira — pending the scope question below. Don't cut them\\nearly and then have to re-scope mid-sprint if the answer changes what \\"qualifying\\" means.)", "section_path": "Story Breakdown"}, {"content": "## Dependencies\\n| Item | Owner | Due |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| D3 indexing pipeline stable enough to extend | Relay (Jason Maro) | Already met |\\n| Confirmation of \\"qualifying PR\\" definition | Dana Whitfield (client) | See Open Questions |", "section_path": "Dependencies"}, {"content": "## Open Questions\\n- OQ-01: Does \\"assisted capture\\" include drafting from long PR **comment threads**\\n  post-merge, not just the diff + description? Raised informally by client (Slack via Dana,\\n  2026-09-03). Materially changes story-point estimate (comment-thread extraction is a\\n  different, harder extraction problem than PR description parsing). **Decision deadline:\\n  2026-09-19** — if unresolved, this epic does not start on schedule and D8's Nov 30 date\\n  is at risk. Owner: A. Gupta + Dana Whitfield. If the answer expands scope, this needs a\\n  formal CR, not just an epic-brief footnote.", "section_path": "Open Questions"}, {"content": "## Risks\\nSee R-03 in the Risk & Issue Log (scope ambiguity, same underlying question as OQ-01).", "section_path": "Risks"}, {"content": "## Estimate & Timeline\\n19 points as scoped today (excludes comment-thread extraction). Earliest start: once OQ-01\\nresolves. At current team velocity (~24 pts/sprint across the whole team, not just this\\nepic), this fits in one sprint once unblocked — the risk is entirely the open question, not\\nthe build.", "section_path": "Estimate & Timeline"}]
196113dc-4ce4-46fb-88d6-f65b0e0735e7	acme-data-migration-20d649	sprint_planning	\N	internal	1.0	2026-09-14	A. Gupta	final	2026-09-15	t	07_sprint_planning_sprint14.md	/Users/anyagupta/Documents/idea-explainer-pro/backend/storage/pm_documents/acme-data-migration-20d649/196113dc-4ce4-46fb-88d6-f65b0e0735e7.md	0fb8fb24898c775881da823962482ac496c9fbb70dff96918c614ef607087a75	confirmed	1	Front matter present and valid — deterministic parse, no LLM call.	\N	{"people": [], "cr_refs": ["CR-002"], "risk_ids": ["R-01"], "ticket_refs": ["KPD-101", "KPD-11", "KPD-127", "KPD-133", "KPD-247"], "decision_ids": [], "deliverable_ids": ["D2", "D3", "D5", "D6", "D8"], "requirement_ids": []}	agupta	2026-09-14 17:26:16.160706+00	agupta	2026-09-14 17:30:38.9492+00	[{"content": "# Sprint 14 Planning Notes", "section_path": "(preamble)"}, {"content": "## Header\\nSprint 14 · 2026-09-15 → 2026-09-26 · Planning held 2026-09-14\\nAttendees: A. Gupta, Akshar Kher, Jason Maro, Omar K, Priya Kumar, Shubhr Aryan\\nAbsent: Agrim Gairola (personal leave, started 2026-09-08, expected back ~2026-09-29 —\\nsee R-01 in risk log; his in-flight D5/D3-adjacent tickets were reassigned, not deferred,\\nper the note below)\\nCapacity: 5 of 6 engineers available (Agrim out) → capacity calc 32 pts (down from usual\\n~40; not fully reduced 1/6 since two of his tickets were already near-done and just needed\\nsomeone else to finish, not restart)\\nCommitted velocity target: 30 pts (leaving buffer given last sprint ran over — see Sprint 13\\nretro, \\"what went poorly\\")", "section_path": "Header"}, {"content": "## Sprint Backlog\\n| Story ID | Title | Pts |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| KPD-127 | SOW deliverable mapping for D3 out of date after classifier rewrite | 3 |\\n| KPD-133 | Written definition of ambiguous vs out-of-scope — remaining edge cases | 2 |\\n| KPD-101 | Ask endpoint returns 500 instead of 429 when downstream rate limit hit | 3 |\\n| KPD-11 | Comment ingestion truncates bodies over 32KB instead of paginating | 5 |\\n| — | D6 revocation-lag fix (KPD-247) re-verification against full regression suite | 5 |\\n| — | D2 linkage: pick up remaining commit-convention edge cases post-CR-002 | 8 |\\n| — | D8 epic: blocked pending OQ-01 (see Epic Brief EPIC-D8) — not pulled into backlog | 0 |\\n\\nTotal: 26 pts pulled against a 30 pt target — deliberately left ~4 pts of slack given the\\nAgrim gap and because KPD-127 (reassigned from Agrim) may take longer for someone unfamiliar\\nwith that code path to pick up cleanly.", "section_path": "Sprint Backlog"}, {"content": "## Dependencies Pulled In\\n- Dana Whitfield's answer on OQ-01 (D8 scope) — needed by 2026-09-19 per the epic brief;\\n  not a blocker for this sprint's committed work, but flagged so nobody quietly starts D8\\n  prep work before it resolves.", "section_path": "Dependencies Pulled In"}, {"content": "## Definition of Done\\nStandard project DoD applies (stored once in project config, not restated per sprint) — code\\nreviewed, tests passing, deployed to staging, ticket linked to its commit for D2 coverage\\npurposes(!), acceptance criteria checked off by the ticket owner before moving to Done.", "section_path": "Definition of Done"}]
ff9f9892-88cc-4643-9a37-2f5d1043a8ac	acme-data-migration-20d649	status_report	\N	client	1.0	2026-09-14	A. Gupta	final	2026-09-08	f	10_status_report_2026-09-08.md	/Users/anyagupta/Documents/idea-explainer-pro/backend/storage/pm_documents/acme-data-migration-20d649/ff9f9892-88cc-4643-9a37-2f5d1043a8ac.md	51815de1a253b388f01b7a019b47e87b298479e74812dfd39eb059fb817ca79b	confirmed	1	Front matter present and valid — deterministic parse, no LLM call.	\N	{"people": [], "cr_refs": ["CR-002"], "risk_ids": ["I-04", "R-01", "R-02", "R-03"], "ticket_refs": ["KPD-101"], "decision_ids": [], "deliverable_ids": ["D1", "D2", "D3", "D4", "D5", "D6", "D7", "D8"], "requirement_ids": []}	agupta	2026-09-14 17:25:43.968868+00	agupta	2026-09-14 17:27:17.831044+00	[{"content": "# Weekly Status Report — Week of 2026-09-08", "section_path": "(preamble)"}, {"content": "## Overall Status\\n🟡 Amber — D6 shipped a key fix, D5's classifier rework landed, but D2 remains behind its\\nrevised date and D8 hasn't started pending a scope answer. Nothing client-blocking, but two\\nof eight deliverables need attention to avoid the Nov 30 end date slipping.", "section_path": "Overall Status"}, {"content": "## Progress\\n21 points completed this week (partial-week measurement; see Sprint 13 Review for the full\\nsprint number — 24/28, 86%). % spend vs. plan: 22.5% of contract value invoiced\\n($48,100 of $214,000) against ~69% of calendar elapsed (kickoff 2026-03-02, planned end\\n2026-11-30) — invoicing lags calendar because it's tied to deliverable acceptance, not time,\\nand only D1 has been formally accepted so far. This gap is expected to close as D5/D6/D7\\napproach acceptance in the next 4–6 weeks, but it's worth being upfront that it looks worse\\non a simple % basis than the underlying progress actually is.", "section_path": "Progress"}, {"content": "## Milestone Health\\n| Milestone | RAG |\\n|---|---|\\n| D1 | 🟢 Accepted |\\n| D2 | 🟡 Behind revised date (CR-002); see R-02 |\\n| D3 | 🟢 On track |\\n| D4 | 🟡 Not started yet, spec-only this sprint |\\n| D5 | 🟢 On track, classifier rework shipped |\\n| D6 | 🟢 Critical fix shipped, pending security sign-off |\\n| D7 | 🟢 Near acceptance |\\n| D8 | 🔴 Not started — scope question open, see R-03 |", "section_path": "Milestone Health"}, {"content": "## Top Risks & Issues\\nSee Risk & Issue Log for full detail (single-writer rule) — currently active: R-01\\n(key-person coverage gap), R-02 (D2 schedule), R-03 (D8 scope ambiguity), I-04 (rate-limit\\nbug KPD-101, in progress).", "section_path": "Top Risks & Issues"}, {"content": "## This Week / Next Week\\nThis week: D6 revocation fix, D5 classifier rework, D4 spec written.\\nNext week (Sprint 14): D2 convention edge cases, KPD-101 rate-limit fix, D6 re-verification\\nagainst full regression suite, Agrim's reassigned tickets in progress with new owners.", "section_path": "This Week / Next Week"}, {"content": "## Client Asks\\n- Dana asked for D2 coverage-number transparency going forward (see retro action item —\\n  will send a short async note whenever a CR changes something, not just the formal doc).\\n- OQ-01 (D8 scope — comment-thread drafts) still needs Dana's written answer; deadline\\n  2026-09-19 per the D8 epic brief.", "section_path": "Client Asks"}, {"content": "## Budget Snapshot\\nInvoiced to date: $48,100 (signing 15% + D1 milestone). Remaining: $165,900 across D2–D8.\\nNo cost overruns to report — CR-002's extra effort was absorbed at no charge per its\\ndisposition.", "section_path": "Budget Snapshot"}]
ab6ad637-917e-4ee4-8dd9-a12e3bf2efc9	acme-data-migration-20d649	uat_signoff	UAT-D1	client	1.0	2026-04-24	A. Gupta	final	\N	f	12_uat_signoff_d1.md	/Users/anyagupta/Documents/idea-explainer-pro/backend/storage/pm_documents/acme-data-migration-20d649/ab6ad637-917e-4ee4-8dd9-a12e3bf2efc9.md	9de5904f35cde069706e18530f50bf0f414f35dec59759d7688b1f84f3d1cfcf	confirmed	1	Front matter present and valid — deterministic parse, no LLM call.	\N	{"people": [], "cr_refs": [], "risk_ids": ["I-05"], "ticket_refs": ["KPD-14", "KPD-27"], "decision_ids": [], "deliverable_ids": ["D1"], "requirement_ids": []}	agupta	2026-09-14 17:25:44.004046+00	agupta	2026-09-14 17:27:18.045611+00	[{"content": "# UAT Sign-off — D1: Data Ingestion Connectors", "section_path": "(preamble)"}, {"content": "## Deliverable\\nD1 — Data Ingestion Connectors (Jira + GitHub)", "section_path": "Deliverable"}, {"content": "## Review Against Acceptance Criteria\\n- Sync within 5 minutes of a change: **Met** — verified against 12 live changes during UAT\\n  window (avg 2m10s).\\n- Full historical backfill without manual intervention: **Met**.\\n- Webhook delivery survives bursts of 50+ events/minute: **Met**, though see condition below\\n  — this was re-tested harder post-signoff after KPD-27/33 surfaced a related burst bug in\\n  the (separate) webhook-to-Jira-sync path, not this ingestion connector itself.\\n- Attachment metadata, including non-UTF8 filenames, ingests without silent failure:\\n  **Accepted with condition** — one edge case found during UAT (a filename with a\\n  right-to-left Unicode override character) failed silently instead of erroring loudly.\\n  Not a blocker for acceptance since the *common* non-UTF8 case (accented Latin filenames)\\n  worked correctly, but tracked as a condition rather than waved through silently.\\n\\n**Outcome: Accepted with conditions.**\\n\\nCondition: fix the RTL-override filename edge case within 2 sprints of sign-off, tracked as\\nKPD-14. Resolved 2026-05-06 (see Risk & Issue Log I-05, Closed) — condition satisfied.", "section_path": "Review Against Acceptance Criteria"}, {"content": "## Invoice Authorization\\nMilestone: D1, 8.4% of contract value (per SOW milestone table) → **$16,000** authorized for\\ninvoicing upon this sign-off, per the Deliverables Matrix.", "section_path": "Invoice Authorization"}, {"content": "## Signatures\\n- Dana Whitfield, Program Manager, Arclight Systems — 2026-04-24\\n- Marcus Feld, VP Engineering, Arclight Systems — 2026-04-24\\n- Anya Gupta, Delivery Lead, Relay Labs — 2026-04-24", "section_path": "Signatures"}]
084eab81-df1f-47cc-9543-ed6345a33bac	acme-data-migration-20d649	meeting_notes	\N	client	1.0	2026-09-10	A. Gupta	final	2026-09-10	t	13_meeting_notes_2026-09-10_client_sync.md	/Users/anyagupta/Documents/idea-explainer-pro/backend/storage/pm_documents/acme-data-migration-20d649/084eab81-df1f-47cc-9543-ed6345a33bac.md	e17e6aa74b891f90d83301a98da67488ffc5ca28215046203ef54c60c0fc5ade	confirmed	1	Front matter present and valid — deterministic parse, no LLM call.	\N	{"people": [], "cr_refs": ["CR-002"], "risk_ids": [], "ticket_refs": ["KPD-247"], "decision_ids": ["D-01", "D-02"], "deliverable_ids": ["D2", "D6", "D8"], "requirement_ids": []}	agupta	2026-09-14 17:26:16.319243+00	agupta	2026-09-14 17:30:39.112623+00	[{"content": "# Meeting Notes — Arclight Client Sync", "section_path": "(preamble)"}, {"content": "## Header\\nType: Recurring biweekly client sync · Date: 2026-09-10, 30 min\\nAttendees: A. Gupta, Dana Whitfield, Marcus Feld (first 10 min only, dropped for another\\ncall), Chris Okafor (joined for the D6 discussion, left after)\\nFacilitator: A. Gupta", "section_path": "Header"}, {"content": "## Agenda\\n1. D6 revocation-lag fix — security review path\\n2. D2 status (carried over from last sync, Dana had follow-up questions)\\n3. D8 scope question — need Dana's answer\\n4. Agrim's leave — any client-visible impact?", "section_path": "Agenda"}, {"content": "## Decisions\\n- D-01: Chris Okafor will do the D6 security review async this week rather than waiting for\\n  the next sync — no need to block two more weeks just to get a meeting slot. Fix (KPD-247)\\n  doesn't count toward D6 acceptance until he signs off.\\n- D-02: Dana will get a written answer on OQ-01 (D8 comment-thread scope) to us by\\n  2026-09-19 as planned; she flagged that internally it might need a quick legal look if it\\n  changes what counts as \\"captured\\" content, so the date could slip a few days — noted, not\\n  pushing back on it since it's their internal process, not ours to rush.", "section_path": "Decisions"}, {"content": "## Action Items\\n| Item | Owner | Due |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Send Chris the D6 regression suite results + repro steps for KPD-247 | Jason Maro | 2026-09-11 |\\n| Written OQ-01 answer | Dana Whitfield | 2026-09-19 (may slip a few days, see D-02) |\\n| Short async note explaining what CR-002 did and didn't fix for D2 (per Sprint 13 retro) | A. Gupta | 2026-09-11 |", "section_path": "Action Items"}, {"content": "## Blockers\\nNone client-blocking this week. Internally, D8 can't start until OQ-01 resolves (tracked in\\nEpic Brief EPIC-D8, not restated here).", "section_path": "Blockers"}, {"content": "## Parking Lot\\n- Dana asked (again, informally) about exposing the Scope Guardian \\"ambiguous\\" reason text\\n  to her team directly. Same ask as the Sprint 13 review parking lot — noting here too since\\n  she brought it up unprompted a second time, which probably means it matters more to her\\n  than a single parking-lot mention suggested. Worth a real answer next sync instead of\\n  parking it twice.\\n- Marcus asked in passing (before dropping off) whether Continuity could eventually pull in\\n  Confluence too. Not scoped, not in the SOW, no commitment made — flagged only because it's\\n  the kind of thing that quietly becomes an expectation if nobody writes it down as *not*\\n  agreed to.", "section_path": "Parking Lot"}]
