umber still looked lower than expected\\n  given CR-002 was supposed to have fixed the convention-matching gap. Mapped to KPD-115/123\\n  — those are still in progress, CR-002 approved the *date*, not a claim that the work was\\n  already done by that date. Logged as a communication gap to fix, not a technical one — see\\n  retro.\\n- Parking lot: Dana asked if the classifier's \\"ambiguous\\" reason text could be exposed to\\n  her team directly rather than only to the internal PM view. Not scoped in D5's SOW acceptance\\n  criteria as written; noted for a possible CR if she wants to pursue it, not committed to.", "section_path": "Feedback & Requests"}, {"content": "## Metrics Update\\nVelocity: 24 pts completed against a 28 pt commitment (86%) — third sprint in a row under\\ncommitment; see retro action items. Milestone health: D1 accepted, D5/D6 tracking to\\n2026-09-30, D2 still amber (see Deliverables Matrix and R-02).", "section_path": "Metrics Update"}]
