everyone owns a distinct area.\\n- Client communication gap: Dana was surprised D2's coverage number hadn't moved much since\\n  CR-002, because nobody proactively told her CR-002 fixed the *date*, not the *progress* —\\n  she reasonably assumed approving a CR meant the underlying problem was already solved.", "section_path": "What Went Poorly"}, {"content": "## Action Items\\n| Action | Owner | Due |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Add a rough \\"handoff readiness\\" check to sprint planning for anyone with planned time off | A. Gupta | 2026-09-26 (next planning) |\\n| Send Dana a short async update whenever a CR is approved, separate from the formal doc, clarifying what actually changes near-term | A. Gupta | Immediate / ongoing |\\n| Pad new estimates for D2-adjacent linkage work by 20% until convention-discovery rate drops | Jason Maro | Sprint 14 |\\n| Revisit whether \\"ambiguous\\" reason text should be client-facing (Dana's parking-lot ask) | A. Gupta | 2026-09-30 |", "section_path": "Action Items"}]
