83240bcb-a3dc-4281-9481-a793f57d2169	9e69ad9a-be07-4f6a-8690-0da3936389c9	assistant	The work addressed two bugs: KPD‑169, which involved a provenance‑check that incorrectly allowed a read operation [421fe2b25730c9ea55c2554c46d08af1d0251354], and KPD‑18, which concerned incorrect label changes on JIRA issue #47 [86eaa944887d3a9dd5baa9040cff91efa177fd68][8d83c0017e704c556071baa59a18129b7eb32949][a2efba31ba4ae4c1aa973aa6b991257e33ed81e8]. The code changes were a series of clean‑up commits that applied fixes for these problems, each prefixed with “clean up fixkpd…”, identified by the four commit hashes listed above. These commits modify the relevant modules to enforce the correct provenance check and to correct the label‑handling logic for the affected JIRA issue.	{88fcab69-27b0-4a6e-805c-ac0c13551980,6d6903df-b6cc-48ab-bbf6-7f872926e402,9efafbc8-0da3-4c16-8de0-371e4a3e027a,4b74f04b-196c-4eaf-acb1-76f25223872f}	f	2026-09-11 12:00:36.896095+00	\N	\N	\N	\N
