c9cd1b42-7984-460d-805a-46736b286ee6	1ad72c33-bcd5-4896-b7dc-db9269ccc16c	assistant	Priya has wrapped up a series of bug investigations and fixes focused on UI overflow, spinner behavior, chart labeling, security checks, and multiple canary‑token related regressions.  \n- KPD-239: Fixed filter chips overflowing off‑screen on the epics dashboard at 1280 px, restoring usable navigation on smaller viewports. [KPD-239]  \n- KPD-238: Resolved Scope Guardian upload spinner not clearing after a failed SOW parse, preventing indefinite loading states for users. [KPD-238]  \n- KPD-236: Corrected coverage donut chart mislabeling of the unlinked slice on narrow viewports, ensuring accurate data visualization. [KPD-236]  \n- KPD-190: Investigated canary‑token triggers during seeder test runs to determine race or stale‑cache causes, improving test reliability. [KPD-190]  \n- KPD-188: Fixed provenance check that incorrectly allowed reads with expired but not‑yet‑revoked API keys, closing a security gap and unblocking secrets‑scanner cleanup. [KPD-188]  \n- KPD-187: Addressed canary‑token trigger regression after reindex affecting the linkage job, needed for correct evaluation harness results. [KPD-187]  \n- KPD-177: Fixed missing alerts when the webhook endpoint is unreachable, restoring alerting reliability for canary‑token triggers. [KPD-177]  \n- KPD-170: Resolved 500 error with no stack trace during canary‑token test runs on the handover brief endpoint, aiding debugging and system stability. [KPD-170]	{bbafa041-9fb2-4144-97a9-03260f444253,df733c86-fd46-4ef4-857f-c764d6b93068,6dccfa6f-2044-40ee-b7ed-2acd27881e7a,439cc6cb-a9ac-427a-82ce-b8c178218423,bca567d6-b1bd-4463-a348-0bc435920e90,ae7a1ea7-f119-407d-905c-22e5eefd54f4,f79adf83-0b11-41f9-9a2d-5845f59b846e,66e2c497-93a4-4dbf-a43c-27ba83216378}	f	2026-09-14 15:13:02.496558+00	cache	81	8	\N
