11af7809-aad4-4cfb-816c-3af4695be6b8	af02deac-4f32-4edd-97cb-f3c4f2613105	assistant	Agrim's open tickets concentrate on reliability, error-handling, and security gaps that are causing flaky CI runs, resource exhaustion, and inconsistent service behavior.\n\n- KPD-225: GitHub rate-limit handling ignores the secondary limit on the PR review endpoint, leading to inconsistent results under load; fixing it will prevent API throttling failures. [KPD-225]\n- KPD-216: Deploy pipeline lacks automatic rollback on a failed health check, risking prolonged exposure to broken releases; adding rollback will improve production stability. [KPD-216]\n- KPD-211: CI pipeline flakes on the eval stage (~12% of runs) and the handover-brief endpoint throws ConnectionPoolExhausted instead of degrading gracefully; stabilizing this will make test results trustworthy. [KPD-211]\n- KPD-205: CI runner runs out of memory during the embedding batch test as the corpus fixture grew, causing test crashes; addressing OOM will keep CI reliable for large data sets. [KPD-205]\n- KPD-202: Auth provider webhook signature verification is skipped in one code path, resulting in a 500 error with no stack trace; correcting this secures authentication flows. [KPD-202]\n- KPD-201: Auth provider webhook signature verification is also skipped during a schema migration, producing a stale-cache hit instead of the expected response; fixing it ensures consistent retrieval service behavior. [KPD-201]\n- KPD-178: Canary-token trigger fails to fire an alert when the webhook endpoint is unreachable, weakening incident detection; restoring the alert will improve monitoring reliability. [KPD-178]	{d3eb3c08-c059-4f3d-b8ab-acbcef31dbff,f229eaa4-443a-43c7-a111-eb00f041fb19,dcb3743f-f8c8-4e3f-825a-e3dc855ffc7d,ff247cac-738c-49f5-a13b-4e6bcf02a5e6,3ee64df6-b1ff-4443-a37a-15bd09949f98,6366d7a0-a7e2-4f44-a195-637f4edeb9fa,16b3f429-08f3-4c1a-ba63-443c58aad786}	f	2026-09-14 20:35:50.101399+00	groq	1927	7	\N
