32111876-5747-491c-9120-f3f3f01c835e	af02deac-4f32-4edd-97cb-f3c4f2613105	assistant	The PRD for the Scope Guardian (D5) defines a set of concrete goals for the feature:\n\n- Automatic SOW parsing - When a Statement of Work is uploaded (PDF or pasted text), the system must extract the document’s deliverables and acceptance criteria into a structured, editable list [94fb37fc-2436-4fd9-8110-493881850d7d].\n- Ticket/PR classification - Using the parsed SOW, incoming tickets or pull-requests are automatically classified as in-scope, out-of-scope, or ambiguous [94fb37fc-2436-4fd9-8110-493881850d7d].\n- Human-in-the-loop validation - The generated deliverable list is presented to the product manager for confirmation before it becomes live, ensuring that any classification decisions that need judgment are surfaced to a human manager [94fb37fc-2436-4fd9-8110-493881850d7d].\n- Scope-only focus - The feature is limited to classifying against an already-agreed SOW; it does not perform legal review, contract redlining, or automatically close out-of-scope tickets [94fb37fc-2436-4fd9-8110-493881850d7d].\n\nThese goals together aim to streamline decision-making around what work is covered by the contract while keeping final authority with the project manager. (The PRD itself is referenced as [PRD-D5-01].)	{de31254b-cd2c-4aad-8323-312a1a304e0b,5d98d86e-77fc-45d1-b565-b7aa3c6f9d86,ffda3a27-41e8-4660-bbaf-4737f4463163,a8b67746-4e8f-476c-b118-8685a330e5fc}	f	2026-09-15 09:13:03.731386+00	groq	2580	4	\N
